# Infrastructure

- EF configs: `Infrastructure/Persistence/Configurations/` implementing `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` (auto-discovered).
- Repos: `Infrastructure/Persistence/Repositories/`. `Repository<TEntity> where TEntity : BaseEntity` is the shared generic base (composable `Query`/`QueryAsNoTracking`, `GetByIdAsync`, `FirstOrDefaultAsync`, `SingleOrDefaultAsync`, `ListAsync`, `PageAsync`, `AnyAsync`, `CountAsync`, add/update/remove incl. range variants) and works for **any** entity, aggregate root or not. All members are `virtual`; a per-entity repository overrides or adds intention-revealing methods. `Currency`/`LoanType` currently have no repository — they are read through query handlers projecting from `IApplicationDbContext` — but nothing stops one being added now.
- Messages thrown from here are **localization keys**, never sentences: `throw new DomainValidationException("InvalidPageSize")`. Do not inject `IStringLocalizer` into a repository or service — the WebApi exception filter resolves the key. See `.cursor/rules/localization.mdc`.
- **Includes are a shaper, never a string**: `include: q => q.Include(a => a.Currency).ThenInclude(...)`. The old comma-separated `includeProperties` silently returned unloaded navigations on a typo; the delegate is compiler-checked and survives renames.
- **`Update` deliberately does nothing when the aggregate is already tracked.** `DbSet.Update` marks every property modified, rewriting untouched columns and churning the `RowVersion` token. `Repository.Update` only calls it for a `Detached` entity — the disconnected case where there is no tracked original to diff. Same shape in `Remove` (attach first if detached).
- Reads default to **tracked** (`asNoTracking: false`). A silently-dropped mutation is a bug; a redundant tracking entry is a perf nit. Pass `asNoTracking: true` for read-only paths.
- `PageAsync` returns `(Items, TotalCount)` derived from one filter, so the count and the page cannot drift apart. The count is composed **without** the ordering or the include shaper (neither can change `COUNT(*)`), and when no `orderBy` is supplied it falls back to ordering by `Id` — `Skip`/`Take` with no ordering makes EF emit `ORDER BY (SELECT 1)`, which lets the server repeat a row across pages and drop another entirely.
- **`PageAsync` materialises entities.** For a read endpoint prefer paging in the query handler with `ProjectTo` (see `GetApplicationsQuery`) — going through `PageAsync` to build a DTO list loads every column of every row and then throws most of it away. Both paging paths are correct; pick by whether you need the aggregate or a projection.
- `UnitOfWork` is a single-field class over `IApplicationDbContext` exposing `SaveChangesAsync`. Do **not** add repository properties to it, and do not make its members `virtual` — tests mock `IUnitOfWork`, not the concrete class.
- `GetByIdAsync` passes the key as `new object[] { id }`. `FindAsync(id, cancellationToken)` binds the `params object?[]` overload and silently treats the token as a second key value.
- `ApplicationDbContext` in `Infrastructure/Persistence/`; migrations in `Infrastructure/Migrations/`.
- Identity: `ApplicationUser` + `IdentityService` for identity operations, with token minting split out into `JwtTokenGenerator` (`IJwtTokenGenerator`, singleton; `JwtOptions` bound via `IOptionsMonitor<JwtOptions>` and validated on start). Issuer/audience validation disabled by design in the template.
- **Audit columns are stamped by `AuditableEntityInterceptor`**, not by the entities or handlers. It is resolved from the container, which is why both `AddDbContext` calls use the two-argument `(provider, options)` overload — the single-argument one cannot reach it. It is registered **scoped as a floor, not a requirement**: both its dependencies (`ICurrentUserService`, `IDateTime`) are singletons today, so scoped simply keeps it correct if `ICurrentUserService` ever becomes per-request. Register it on **both** provider branches: attached only to SQL Server, auditing silently stops wherever `UseInMemoryDatabase` is true, tests included. It fills `Created`/`CreatedBy` only where the entity left them unset, so `OtpVerification`'s own values survive. A no-op update writes nothing, so it does **not** bump `LastModified` — though the aggregate still raises its updated event.
- EF mapping lives **only** here. Entities carry no `[ForeignKey]`/`[NotMapped]`; relationships are declared with `HasOne(...).WithMany().HasForeignKey(...)` in the entity configuration.
- DI composition: `AddInfrastructureServices` in `Infrastructure/Common/Extensions/ConfigureServices.cs`. Both aggregate repositories (`ILoanApplicationRepository`, `IOtpVerificationRepository`) and `IUnitOfWork` are registered there as scoped services. Repositories are **not** assembly-scanned; one missing from that list fails to resolve at startup.
- In-memory switch: `UseInMemoryDatabase` from config (honored in that extension).
- New aggregate checklist: mark the root `IAggregateRoot` → domain repository interface → EF configuration → repository impl → DI registration in `AddInfrastructureServices` → inject it into the command handler → migration. Nothing to add to `IUnitOfWork`.
- Replace `LoggingSmsSender` before production SMS; one class + one DI line.
